cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Prometheus: a meta-prompting framework for agentic systems"
message: "If you use this framework in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Samuele Stronati"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Samuele95/prometheus"
url: "https://samuele95.github.io/prometheus/code-forge.html"
abstract: >-
  Prometheus is a build-time meta-prompting framework that designs, audits, and
  refactors prompts for tool-calling LLM agents. It treats a prompt as an
  operator acting on a model's distribution over interpretations rather than a
  key that retrieves a stored answer, and covers seven structural prompt shapes
  across three modes: from-scratch design, refactor, and MAPE-K lifecycle
  management of a deployed agent. Every deliverable ships with a verifier
  specification across static, single-run, and cross-run layers.
keywords:
  - prompt engineering
  - meta-prompting
  - large language models
  - agentic systems
  - LLM-as-judge
  - context engineering
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-25"
